      "cooked": "<p>Had an argument at the table tonight about what happens when Ethereal Bonds is destroyed (\"\n\n\n<span>At the end of the Environment turn, this card deals the Hero Target with the highest HP 2 Energy Damage. A Target dealt Damage this way cannot deal Damage until the start of the next Environment turn.</span>\").&nbsp; One player argued that, since EB was gone, the \"cannot deal damage\" effect was also gone.&nbsp; But it seemed to me that it should still persist until the start of the next Environment turn.&nbsp; I can't quite articulate why I think that, however, so I could perhaps be wrong.&nbsp; Opinions?</p>",
